# APP Production Experience Consistency

See `lib/app-production-experience/`.

## Never show in ordinary customer APP

- QA / smoke / probe users (`oaa-*`, `*-smoke-*`, `*-probe-*`)
- `.invalid` or `example.com` identities
- Phase 620 / `ps620:` / `app_showcase_data_registry` demo rows as real data
- Placeholder pages in nav (`coming soon`, foundation-only shells)
- Raw enums (`pending`, `active`, `action_required`)
- Raw ISO dates
- Raw translation keys or leaf placeholders (`Title`, `Subtitle`, `Label`, `Empty Cta`, `Principle`)
- Mixed language on one page (e.g. English headings in Norwegian UI)
- Stale notifications presented as pending approvals
- Generic sales/USD philosophy copy as the customer’s contracted plan or billing history
- `Aipify Starter` as active plan when the customer has a different contracted plan

## Required contracts

1. **Fixture isolation** — classify via `lib/app-production-experience` and/or `app_showcase_data_registry`; exclude in canonical queries/RPCs. Do not rely on one-off string filters in React components alone.
2. **Route visibility** — `route-readiness.ts` + license/capability/role gates. Hide unfinished routes; redirect portal billing shells to `/app/settings/billing`.
3. **Tenant** — use `resolveAppOrganizationContext` / `requireReadyAppPortalContext`. No first-org fallback, no Platform org, no `my-company-1`.
4. **Counts** — dashboard KPI and list cards for the same domain must share one authoritative aggregate.
5. **Plan / license / package / module** — keep distinct; never conflate licensed capability rows with “Business Packs installed”.
6. **Presentation** — reuse Platform presentation-quality formatters/status labels for dates and statuses; full locale parity for active locales.
7. **i18n splits** — portalStructure pages must load the `portalStructure` dictionary split (never only `dashboard` when reading `customerApp.portalStructure.*`).
8. **Tests** — new APP surfaces need visual/data consistency coverage under `lib/app-production-experience/**` (or domain tests that assert fixture exclusion and readiness).

## Forbidden

- Shipping visible “kommer snart” / phase-placeholder shells in Production nav
- Hardcoding UnoNight (or any customer) IDs in components
- Deleting audit history to “clean” fixtures
- Mutating agreement, license, entitlement, runtime, CMS, auth, or MFA to fix presentation
